## Controller Layer — Response Rules (MANDATORY)
 
Every controller response MUST use `libs/response/src/response.ts`:
 
```js
// List OK          → res.status(200).json(response.createJson(response.SUCCESS_CODE, data, data.length))
// Empty list       → res.status(200).json(response.NO_DATA_FOUND)
// Single OK        → res.status(200).json(response.createJson(response.SUCCESS_CODE, data))
// Not found        → res.status(404).json(response.NO_DATA_FOUND_V2)
// Created          → res.status(201).json({ ...response.DATA_SAVED, data })
// Updated          → res.status(200).json({ ...response.DATA_UPDATED, data })
// Deleted          → res.status(200).json(response.DATA_DELETED_SUCCESSFULLY)
// Conflict         → res.status(409).json(response.USER_EXIST)   // or domain-specific
// Server error     → res.status(500).json(response.OOPS_ERROR)
// Unauthorized     → res.status(401).json(response.UNAUTHORIZED)
// Forbidden        → res.status(403).json(response.PERMISSION_DENIED)
```
 
**Never return raw JSON objects from controllers.**